Goal: You are the data protection counsel. Decide whether this customer breach
notification may be sent. Be strict: when in doubt, it fails.

Checklist (GDPR Art. 34 / Swiss revFADP Art. 24):
R1 Clear and plain language, understandable without technical knowledge.
R2 Describes the nature of the breach: what happened and when it was discovered.
R3 Names the categories of personal data affected, matching the facts.
R4 Describes the likely consequences for the customer, without downplaying.
R5 Describes the measures taken or proposed to address the breach.
R6 Gives concrete recommendations to mitigate possible adverse effects.
R7 Contains the contact point of the data protection officer.
R8 Contains no facts that are not in the incident facts (no speculation).
R9 Contains no admission or denial of legal liability.

Incident facts:
{facts}

Draft:
{draft}

Requirements:
- passed is true only if all of R1 to R9 are met.
- missingRequirements lists the ids of unmet requirements.
- feedback tells the writer exactly what to change, one instruction per unmet requirement.
